              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did namak mean, and what did sābun mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बाल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बाल (bāl) — \"hair\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One hair, and by extension all the hair on a head. Sanskrit vāla, a hair or a horse's tail, stands behind it, and the turn from v- to b- is regular enough between Sanskrit and Hindi that you can use it as a rule of thumb."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take care with its neighbour: bāl- also means 'child' in words borrowed straight from Sanskrit, as in bālak. Those are two different words that happened to fall together in sound, and only the sentence around them says which one is meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five more body words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bāl",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bāl*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bāl, then sābun, so the washing and the washed sit together",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bāl*, then *sābun*, so the washing and the washed sit together]"
            }
          ]
        },
