          "title": "You'll want to know: कान",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कान (kān) — \"an ear\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit karṇa, the ear — also the name of the warrior in the Mahabharata who was born wearing earrings. The path to कान (kān) is the ordinary one: the -rṇ- cluster collapses, the vowel that survives it lengthens, and a two-syllable word becomes one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The same collapse is what turned suvarṇa, 'good colour', into sonā, gold. Once you have seen it twice it stops looking like an accident and starts looking like the machine it is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: hair, a finger, an ear."
            }
          ]
        },
