          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गला",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गला (galā) — \"the throat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit gala, the throat, a cousin of Latin gula, the gullet — the word English took twice over, once as \"gullet\" and once, by a longer road, as \"gluttony\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hindi keeps the plain sense and adds the obvious extension: your गला (galā) is also your voice, and to say that it has gone is to say you have gone hoarse. The organ and what comes out of it share one word, which is a bargain most languages strike somewhere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: hair, a finger, an ear, a nose, the throat."
            }
          ]
        },
